            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "This still needs some work. Sensors can be added and removed during the lifetime of ipmid. So there needs to be a match for interfaces added/removed and possibly re-scanning or rebuilding the threshold match vector."
                },
                {
                    "file": "sensorhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 833,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "bus is a local variable and will be destroyed when the function returns, but the match_t objects in thresholdMatches still hold a reference to it. This will cause a use-after-free crash when a D-Bus signal arrives.\n\nCould you Tell me if my understanding is wrong ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "sensorhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 833,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "bus is just a wrapper created from ipmid_get_sd_bus_connection(), which returns a process-wide shared sd_bus. When the local bus goes out of scope, it does not destroy the underlying D-Bus connection.\nThe match_t objects are effectively tied to that shared global bus, which remains valid for the lifetime of the process. So although it looks like a lifetime issue, it doesn\u2019t lead to a real use-after-free here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "sensorhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 833,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Nagavarapu Sai Pavan",
                        "email": "saipavann@ami.com",
                        "username": "saipavann27"
                    },
                    "message": "Good change. Caching threshold values via D-Bus signals avoids a live D-Bus call on every IPMI request, which should reduce latency by around 10\u201315ms per call."
                }
            ],
